---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import Fill from '../components/Fill.astro';
import { OWNER } from '../config/legal';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Cookie policy"
  description="Which cookies B2BRated sets today, and what we will tell you before that changes."
  path="/cookies"
>
  <h2>Cookies we set today</h2>
  <p>
    None. The site does not set cookies of its own, and it runs no analytics, advertising or tracking tools that set
    them. You can read every page without accepting anything, so there is no cookie banner.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies from other companies</h2>
  <p>
    Pages load fonts, scripts and images from our own site. We do not embed videos, social buttons or ad networks, so no
    outside company sets a cookie through our pages. Links to vendor websites leave this site, and those sites have
    their own cookie rules.
  </p>

  <h2>What will change</h2>
  <p>
    When accounts open, signing in will need a cookie that keeps you logged in. That cookie will be strictly necessary
    for the sign-in to work. If we later add analytics or advertising that use cookies, we will ask for your consent
    first, and we will update this page and the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> before either goes live.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <Fill value={OWNER.email} label="contact email" />, or use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
